  "question": {
    "text": "Corresponding to the process shown in figure, the heat given to the gas in the process&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi><mi>B</mi><mi>C</mi><mi>A</mi></math> is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfenced></math>&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">J</mi></math>. Find value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi></math>.<br />\r<br />\r<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/nta_abhyas/jee_main/images/anjana.PNG\" style=\"width: 390px; height: 230px;\" />",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "5",
  "solution": {
    "text": "Cycle is clockwise. Hence heat will be given to the gas, as work done will be positive.<br /><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Q</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>W</mi><mo>=</mo></math>&nbsp;area of cycle =&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">J</mi></math>",
